v {xschem version=3.4.6 file_version=1.2
* mux2to1_cml (issue #21; generated by design/tx/gen_schematics.py)
*
* Final 2:1 mux (DR-001 decision 2). Two HBT data pairs share resistive
* loads; each pair's tail is a thin-oxide NMOS gated by a rail-swing copy of
* one 5 GHz phase (AC-coupled, self-biased inverter pair squarer).
* Series-gated HBT does not fit the 1.2 V rail (two Vbe + two Vce > 1.2 V),
* hence the MOS tail switch. The clock squarer at 5 GHz is an unproven seam,
* flagged in the sizing record.
*
* First-cut sizing for the PROPOSED draft spec rows; not a spec result and
* not a measurement. Traces to sim/pdk.json.
}
